{
  "levels": [
    {
      "id": "a1-1",
      "name": "A1 · Part 1",
      "schemeLevels": [
        {
          "scheme": "hsk-words",
          "level": "HSK 1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "a1-2",
      "name": "A1 · Part 2",
      "schemeLevels": [
        {
          "scheme": "hsk-words",
          "level": "HSK 1"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "shi",
      "level": "a1-1",
      "title": "是: A is B",
      "summary": "Link two nouns.",
      "pattern": [
        "A + 是 + B"
      ],
      "body": [
        "是 (shì) links two nouns: “A is B”. It is not used before adjectives; for those see the lesson on 很.",
        "To say “is not”, put 不 before it: 不是 (bú shì)."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "id": "shi-1",
          "text": "我是学生。",
          "reading": "wǒ shì xuéshēng.",
          "translation": "I am a student.",
          "focus": "是",
          "distractors": [
            "很",
            "在"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "shi-2",
          "text": "他是老师。",
          "reading": "tā shì lǎoshī.",
          "translation": "He is a teacher.",
          "focus": "是",
          "distractors": [
            "很",
            "在"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "shi-3",
          "text": "这是我的书。",
          "reading": "zhè shì wǒ de shū.",
          "translation": "This is my book.",
          "focus": "是",
          "distractors": [
            "很",
            "吗"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "shi-4",
          "text": "她不是医生。",
          "reading": "tā bú shì yīshēng.",
          "translation": "She is not a doctor.",
          "focus": "是",
          "distractors": [
            "很",
            "在"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bu",
      "level": "a1-1",
      "title": "不: not",
      "summary": "Negate verbs and adjectives.",
      "pattern": [
        "Subject + 不 + Verb / Adjective"
      ],
      "body": [
        "不 (bù) goes directly before the verb or adjective it negates. Before a fourth-tone syllable it is said bú: 不是 bú shì, 不去 bú qù.",
        "For 有 (to have) use 没 instead: 没有."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "id": "bu-1",
          "text": "我不喝牛奶。",
          "reading": "wǒ bù hē niúnǎi.",
          "translation": "I don't drink milk.",
          "focus": "不",
          "distractors": [
            "吗",
            "的"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "bu-2",
          "text": "他不去学校。",
          "reading": "tā bú qù xuéxiào.",
          "translation": "He isn't going to school.",
          "focus": "不",
          "distractors": [
            "吗",
            "的"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "bu-3",
          "text": "今天不冷。",
          "reading": "jīntiān bù lěng.",
          "translation": "It isn't cold today.",
          "focus": "不",
          "distractors": [
            "吗",
            "在"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "bu-4",
          "text": "我们不吃米饭。",
          "reading": "wǒmen bù chī mǐfàn.",
          "translation": "We don't eat rice.",
          "focus": "不",
          "distractors": [
            "吗",
            "的"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ma",
      "level": "a1-1",
      "title": "吗: yes/no questions",
      "summary": "Turn a statement into a question.",
      "pattern": [
        "Statement + 吗？"
      ],
      "body": [
        "Add 吗 (ma) to the end of a statement to turn it into a yes/no question. The word order does not change.",
        "Answer by repeating the verb: 是 or 不是, 喝 or 不喝."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "id": "ma-1",
          "text": "你是学生吗？",
          "reading": "nǐ shì xuéshēng ma?",
          "translation": "Are you a student?",
          "focus": "吗",
          "distractors": [
            "很",
            "也"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "ma-2",
          "text": "你喝茶吗？",
          "reading": "nǐ hē chá ma?",
          "translation": "Do you drink tea?",
          "focus": "吗",
          "distractors": [
            "很",
            "也"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "ma-3",
          "text": "他是中国人吗？",
          "reading": "tā shì Zhōngguórén ma?",
          "translation": "Is he Chinese?",
          "focus": "吗",
          "distractors": [
            "很",
            "也"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "ma-4",
          "text": "你忙吗？",
          "reading": "nǐ máng ma?",
          "translation": "Are you busy?",
          "focus": "吗",
          "distractors": [
            "很",
            "也"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "hen",
      "level": "a1-1",
      "title": "很 + adjective",
      "summary": "Describe things without 是.",
      "pattern": [
        "Subject + 很 + Adjective"
      ],
      "body": [
        "Adjectives work as predicates on their own, without 是. A bare adjective sounds like a comparison, so 很 (hěn) is added; here it often just means “is” rather than “very”.",
        "To negate, use 不 and drop 很: 我不忙."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "id": "hen-1",
          "text": "我很好。",
          "reading": "wǒ hěn hǎo.",
          "translation": "I'm fine.",
          "focus": "很",
          "distractors": [
            "吗",
            "在"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "hen-2",
          "text": "今天很热。",
          "reading": "jīntiān hěn rè.",
          "translation": "It's hot today.",
          "focus": "很",
          "distractors": [
            "吗",
            "在"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "hen-3",
          "text": "这个苹果很大。",
          "reading": "zhège píngguǒ hěn dà.",
          "translation": "This apple is big.",
          "focus": "很",
          "distractors": [
            "吗",
            "在"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "hen-4",
          "text": "米饭很好吃。",
          "reading": "mǐfàn hěn hǎochī.",
          "translation": "The rice is tasty.",
          "focus": "很",
          "distractors": [
            "吗",
            "在"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "de",
      "level": "a1-1",
      "title": "的: possession",
      "summary": "Say whose something is.",
      "pattern": [
        "Owner + 的 + Thing"
      ],
      "body": [
        "的 (de) joins an owner to what it owns, like English ’s.",
        "With close people and groups it is often left out: 我妈妈, 我们学校."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "id": "de-1",
          "text": "这是我的手机。",
          "reading": "zhè shì wǒ de shǒujī.",
          "translation": "This is my phone.",
          "focus": "的",
          "distractors": [
            "很",
            "吗"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "de-2",
          "text": "那是老师的车。",
          "reading": "nà shì lǎoshī de chē.",
          "translation": "That is the teacher's car.",
          "focus": "的",
          "distractors": [
            "很",
            "吗"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "de-3",
          "text": "你的名字很好听。",
          "reading": "nǐ de míngzi hěn hǎotīng.",
          "translation": "Your name sounds nice.",
          "focus": "的",
          "distractors": [
            "很",
            "吗"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "de-4",
          "text": "这是他的朋友。",
          "reading": "zhè shì tā de péngyou.",
          "translation": "This is his friend.",
          "focus": "的",
          "distractors": [
            "很",
            "吗"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ye-dou",
      "level": "a1-2",
      "title": "也 and 都: also, all",
      "summary": "Adverbs before the verb.",
      "pattern": [
        "Subject + 也 / 都 + Verb"
      ],
      "body": [
        "也 (yě, also) and 都 (dōu, all, both) are adverbs: they stand after the subject and before the verb, never at the end of the sentence.",
        "When both are used, 也 comes first: 我们也都去."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "id": "ye-dou-1",
          "text": "我也是学生。",
          "reading": "wǒ yě shì xuéshēng.",
          "translation": "I am a student too.",
          "focus": "也",
          "distractors": [
            "吗",
            "在"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "ye-dou-2",
          "text": "他们都喜欢猫。",
          "reading": "tāmen dōu xǐhuan māo.",
          "translation": "They all like cats.",
          "focus": "都",
          "distractors": [
            "吗",
            "的"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "ye-dou-3",
          "text": "我们都很忙。",
          "reading": "wǒmen dōu hěn máng.",
          "translation": "We are all busy.",
          "focus": "都",
          "distractors": [
            "吗",
            "在"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "ye-dou-4",
          "text": "她也不喝牛奶。",
          "reading": "tā yě bù hē niúnǎi.",
          "translation": "She doesn't drink milk either.",
          "focus": "也",
          "distractors": [
            "吗",
            "的"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ge",
      "level": "a1-2",
      "title": "个: counting things",
      "summary": "Numbers need a measure word.",
      "pattern": [
        "Number / 这 / 那 + 个 + Noun"
      ],
      "body": [
        "Between a number (or 这, 那, 几) and a noun, Chinese needs a measure word. 个 (ge) is the most common one and works with many nouns, especially people.",
        "“Two” before a measure word is 两, not 二: 两个人."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "id": "ge-1",
          "text": "我有一个哥哥。",
          "reading": "wǒ yǒu yí ge gēge.",
          "translation": "I have an older brother.",
          "focus": "个",
          "distractors": [
            "的",
            "很"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "ge-2",
          "text": "这个人很好。",
          "reading": "zhège rén hěn hǎo.",
          "translation": "This person is nice.",
          "focus": "个",
          "distractors": [
            "吗",
            "在"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "ge-3",
          "text": "这里有十个学生。",
          "reading": "zhèlǐ yǒu shí ge xuéshēng.",
          "translation": "There are ten students here.",
          "focus": "个",
          "distractors": [
            "的",
            "很"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "ge-4",
          "text": "我想买两个包子。",
          "reading": "wǒ xiǎng mǎi liǎng ge bāozi.",
          "translation": "I'd like to buy two steamed buns.",
          "focus": "个",
          "distractors": [
            "的",
            "很"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "zai",
      "level": "a1-2",
      "title": "在: where something is",
      "summary": "Say where someone is or does something.",
      "pattern": [
        "Subject + 在 + Place",
        "Subject + 在 + Place + Verb"
      ],
      "body": [
        "在 (zài) says where someone or something is: 我在家. No 是 is needed.",
        "The place comes before the action: 我在家吃饭 (I eat at home)."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "id": "zai-1",
          "text": "我在家。",
          "reading": "wǒ zài jiā.",
          "translation": "I'm at home.",
          "focus": "在",
          "distractors": [
            "是",
            "很"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "zai-2",
          "text": "老师在学校。",
          "reading": "lǎoshī zài xuéxiào.",
          "translation": "The teacher is at school.",
          "focus": "在",
          "distractors": [
            "吗",
            "很"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "zai-3",
          "text": "他在书店看书。",
          "reading": "tā zài shūdiàn kàn shū.",
          "translation": "He reads in the bookshop.",
          "focus": "在",
          "distractors": [
            "吗",
            "很"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "zai-4",
          "text": "我们在饭店吃饭。",
          "reading": "wǒmen zài fàndiàn chī fàn.",
          "translation": "We eat at a restaurant.",
          "focus": "在",
          "distractors": [
            "吗",
            "很"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "you",
      "level": "a1-2",
      "title": "有 and 没有: to have",
      "summary": "Having and “there is”.",
      "pattern": [
        "Subject + 有 + Thing",
        "Subject + 没有 + Thing"
      ],
      "body": [
        "有 (yǒu) means “to have”, and also “there is”: 这里有一个商店.",
        "Its negative is 没有 (méiyǒu), never 不有."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "id": "you-1",
          "text": "我有一只猫。",
          "reading": "wǒ yǒu yì zhī māo.",
          "translation": "I have a cat.",
          "focus": "有",
          "distractors": [
            "在",
            "很"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "you-2",
          "text": "他没有车。",
          "reading": "tā méiyǒu chē.",
          "translation": "He doesn't have a car.",
          "focus": "没有",
          "distractors": [
            "不有",
            "很"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "you-3",
          "text": "这里有一个商店。",
          "reading": "zhèlǐ yǒu yí ge shāngdiàn.",
          "translation": "There is a shop here.",
          "focus": "有",
          "distractors": [
            "很",
            "吗"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "you-4",
          "text": "我没有时间。",
          "reading": "wǒ méiyǒu shíjiān.",
          "translation": "I don't have time.",
          "focus": "没有",
          "distractors": [
            "不有",
            "很"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "le",
      "level": "a1-2",
      "title": "了: it happened",
      "summary": "Mark a completed action.",
      "pattern": [
        "Subject + Verb + 了 + (Object)",
        "Subject + Verb + Object + 了"
      ],
      "body": [
        "了 (le) after a verb marks that the action happened or is complete.",
        "To say it did not happen, use 没 (or 没有) and drop 了: 我没吃.",
        "At the end of the sentence 了 can mark that the situation has now come about: 她去商店了 (she has gone to the shop)."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "id": "le-1",
          "text": "我吃了。",
          "reading": "wǒ chī le.",
          "translation": "I've eaten.",
          "focus": "了",
          "distractors": [
            "很",
            "是"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "le-2",
          "text": "他买了一本书。",
          "reading": "tā mǎi le yì běn shū.",
          "translation": "He bought a book.",
          "focus": "了",
          "distractors": [
            "很",
            "是"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "le-3",
          "text": "我们看了一个电影。",
          "reading": "wǒmen kàn le yí ge diànyǐng.",
          "translation": "We watched a film.",
          "focus": "了",
          "distractors": [
            "很",
            "是"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "le-4",
          "text": "她去商店了。",
          "reading": "tā qù shāngdiàn le.",
          "translation": "She went to the shop.",
          "focus": "了",
          "distractors": [
            "很",
            "是"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
